message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Ansatz Machine: a propose-verify-evolve loop for exact solutions of Einstein's field equations"
abstract: >-
  A research codebase for exact computations in general relativity: symbolic searches for exact vacuum
  solutions, exact Killing-tensor (hidden-symmetry) searches over finite fields, and Morales-Ramis
  (differential Galois) integrability tests of geodesic motion, with pre-registered runs and failed runs kept.
  Its "Only Kerr" axis-integrability results (see ONLY_KERR.md): for stationary axisymmetric vacuum fields with
  Kerr's mass profile and a branched twist deformation, the first-order normal variational equation along the
  lower-axis timelike geodesic has Zariski-dense monodromy for every twist in the physical range at four tested
  spins, so no complete set of meromorphic first integrals exists near that orbit; this is a numerical result
  (50-digit floating point), interval-certified only near the end of the range. A related result, checked by hand
  against Kovacic's algorithm: any stationary axisymmetric vacuum field whose axis function is rational of
  degree at least 3 has Galois group
  SL(2,C) for the axis variational equation at generic energy.
  Developed with substantial assistance from Anthropic's Claude AI models (several versions), which wrote
  most of the code and ran most of the analyses under the author's direction; the author chose the questions,
  directed and reviewed the work, and takes responsibility for its content.
